{
  "title": "The itch and barrier cycle",
  "sources": "47:9,10,11",
  "stages": [
    {
      "start": 0,
      "title": "Barrier",
      "text": "Atopic dermatitis involves epidermal barrier dysfunction and immune dysregulation. Filaggrin alteration is one supplied barrier mechanism."
    },
    {
      "start": 9.26,
      "title": "Scratching",
      "text": "Severe itching drives scratching. Watch the surface become disrupted, followed by a thickened epidermis with repeated scratching. The thickening is lichenification."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.3,
      "title": "Care",
      "text": "Hydration and emollients support barrier care. Distribution changes with age: infants often have face and extensor lesions, while older children favor flexures."
    }
  ],
